# Line-ending and binary policy.
#
# Today this repo behaves correctly only because the maintainer's git has
# core.autocrlf=true. A contributor without it would commit CRLF into blobs and
# break things quietly. This file makes the policy a property of the REPO, so it
# holds regardless of anyone's local git config.
#
# Verified before writing this (against .git/index and the stored blob hashes):
#   - gradlew is stored LF (blob 20913298..., 5321 bytes; the CRLF form would be
#     5490 bytes and a different hash). CRLF here means "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M"
#     on Linux/macOS, so the eol=lf below is load-bearing, not cosmetic.
#   - funkodex_base_catalog.json.gz_ is real gzip (magic 1f8b) and contains NUL
#     bytes, so git's heuristic already treats it as binary. Declaring it binary
#     makes that guaranteed rather than inferred -- eol conversion would corrupt
#     the archive, and DEC-027 already establishes that this asset's exact bytes
#     (including the trailing-underscore name) are load-bearing.

# Normalise text to LF in the repository; check out per the platform.
* text=auto

# Scripts whose ending is functional, not stylistic.
gradlew     text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf

# Never touch these.
*.gz_   binary
*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary
*.jar   binary
*.apk   binary
*.aab   binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.sqlite3 binary
